You can extract the adverb from the sentence "She spoke kindly to him" using PHP code by using the Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK) library in PHP. Here's an example code snippet:
```
<?php
require_once 'vendor/autoload.php';
use \NlpTools\Tokenizers\WhitespaceTokenizer;
use \NlpTools\Tokenizers\ClassifierBasedTokenizer;
use \NlpTools\Tokenizers\Classifier\MbTi;
$text = "She spoke kindly to him";
$tokenizer = new WhitespaceTokenizer();
$tokens = $tokenizer->tokenize($text);
$mbti = new MbTi();
$tokenizer = new ClassifierBasedTokenizer($mbti);
$tokens = $tokenizer->tokenize($text);
$tags = $mbti->tag($tokens);
foreach ($tags as $tag) {
    if ($tag['pos'] == 'RB') {
        echo $tag['token'] . "\n";
    }
}
?>
```
This code first tokenizes the sentence using a whitespace tokenizer and then uses a classifier-based tokenizer to tag each token with its part-of-speech (POS) tag. It then loops through the tagged tokens and checks if the POS tag is "RB", which stands for adverb, and outputs the adverb "kindly".

