What are the best practices for storing fresh produce in the refrigerator using JavaScript code?
To ensure the freshness and longevity of your produce, it's important to store them properly in the refrigerator. Here are some tips:
- Keep fruits and vegetables separate, as fruits produce ethylene gas that can cause vegetables to spoil faster.
- Store leafy greens in a plastic bag with some air holes to prevent wilting.
- Store carrots, celery, and other root vegetables in a damp paper towel to prevent them from drying out.
- Keep mushrooms in a brown paper bag to prevent moisture buildup.
- Store fruits and vegetables in the crisper drawer, which has a higher humidity level.
Here's an example of how you can implement some of these tips in JavaScript code:
// Keep fruits and vegetables separate
const fruits = ['apple', 'banana', 'orange'];
const vegetables = ['carrot', 'broccoli', 'lettuce'];
// Store leafy greens in a plastic bag
const greens = ['spinach', 'kale', 'arugula'];
const bag = document.createElement('div');
bag.style = 'background-color: green; width: 100px; height: 100px; padding: 10px;';
greens.forEach(green => {
  const item = document.createElement('p');
  item.innerText = green;
  bag.appendChild(item);
});
document.body.appendChild(bag);
// Store carrots in a damp paper towel
const carrots = ['baby carrot', 'full-size carrot'];
const towel = document.createElement('div');
towel.style = 'background-color: beige; width: 100px; height: 100px; padding: 10px;';
carrots.forEach(carrot => {
  const item = document.createElement('p');
  item.innerText = carrot;
  towel.appendChild(item);
});
const dampTowel = document.createElement('div');
dampTowel.style = 'background-color: lightblue; width: 100px; height: 100px; padding: 10px;';
dampTowel.appendChild(towel);
document.body.appendChild(dampTowel);
// Keep mushrooms in a brown paper bag
const mushrooms = ['button mushroom', 'shiitake', 'portobello'];
const paperBag = document.createElement('div');
paperBag.style = 'background-color: brown; width: 100px; height: 100px; padding: 10px;';
mushrooms.forEach(mushroom => {
  const item = document.createElement('p');
  item.innerText = mushroom;
  paperBag.appendChild(item);
});
document.body.appendChild(paperBag);
// Store fruits and vegetables in the crisper drawer
const crisper = document.createElement('div');
crisper.style = 'background-color: lightgreen; width: 200px; height: 100px; padding: 10px;';
fruits.forEach(fruit => {
  const item = document.createElement('p');
  item.innerText = fruit;
  crisper.appendChild(item);
});
vegetables.forEach(vegetable => {
  const item = document.createElement('p');
  item.innerText = vegetable;
  crisper.appendChild(item);
});
document.body.appendChild(crisper);
By following these storage tips, you can ensure that your produce stays fresh and tasty for longer periods of time.

