How can we expand a linear equation to n variables and ensure that the Gaussian elimination method is utilized for obtaining the solution vector x? Furthermore, can you provide a table that compares the efficiency of different matrix factorization algorithms used in solving systems of linear equations? Please also consider the impact of precision errors and round-off errors when performing the computations. Lastly, can you demonstrate the implementation of the Gaussian elimination method in Python using the following code snippet?
```python
def gaussian_elimination(A, b):
    n = len(A)
    for i in range(n):
        maxrow = i
        for j in range(i+1, n):
            if abs(A[j][i]) > abs(A[maxrow][i]):
                maxrow = j
        A[i], A[maxrow] = A[maxrow], A[i]
        b[i], b[maxrow] = b[maxrow], b[i]
        for j in range(i+1, n):
            c = A[j][i] / A[i][i]
            for k in range(i, n):
                A[j][k] -= c * A[i][k]
            b[j] -= c * b[i]
    x = [0] * n
    for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):
        s = sum(A[i][j] * x[j] for j in range(i, n))
        x[i] = (b[i] - s) / A[i][i]
    return x
```

